  "note": "Poll on Wednesday 18 May 1955; 73.2 per cent polled. Six candidates for four seats in the South-West (Banbrook) ward. T. M'Laughlin's Independent party won all its contests; P. Agnew led the Armagh Labour Party. M'Laughlin, M'Kenna and Agnew were retiring members. Francis W. M'Kee, a former councillor, stood as an Independent."
